_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY2NzI3NzEw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/66727710?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon","html_url":"https://github.com/Mickeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mickeon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-10T10:21:25Z","updated_at":"2025-06-10T10:21:25Z","body":"The existence of this PR fascinates me, because I somewhat assumed this method did not exist for consistency with Node's own API, where adding and moving are separate methods, as well.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2958552302/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2961270413","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106707#issuecomment-2961270413","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106707","id":2961270413,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wgWaN","user":{"login":"djdanlib","id":3030321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzAzMjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3030321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib","html_url":"https://github.com/djdanlib","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T05:15:18Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T05:15:18Z","body":"Should I also do an `insert_icon_item` to match `add_icon_item` for completeness?\r\n\r\nRespect to the real Godot devs here, I feel like such an imposter!\r\n\r\nI consider a list box in any UI toolkit to be an interface to a collection. Some toolkits expose the underlying collection. When they don't, I'd typically want access to basic collection methods.\r\n\r\nThis certainly could be done in a way that keeps the context visually clean by refactoring those two lines out to a helper class. That's what I was about to do before going this route. You'd lose even more efficiency than just using those two lines though. Now you have a new class involved, which feels cluttery, like work I shouldn't be doing. Then you've spent time to write a class, added performance overhead, and added mental overhead. I'm all for reducing complexity. Let's put more wind in a dev's sails, which drives adoption and potential contribution, right?\r\n\r\nYou're right, there isn't exactly a similar thing in `Node`. That's a little surprising if you assume the point of view of someone who just wants to sit down and make stuff. Maybe it's just because nobody's done it yet? `Node` has an indexed `get_child` and `move_child`, and if you tracked/iterated children (which are both annoying things to have to do) you could use `add_sibling`, but there isn't something that maps directly to the concept of an indexed insert. (There also isn't a corresponding indexed remove child operation.) It could be done, I suppose, but to me that looks difficult. Node uses a HashMap for its children under the hood. I'm not brave enough to attempt the level of change it looks like an indexed insert would entail - seems to be a fairly lengthy stack of functions would have to be modified. And I might just be rambling off-topic.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2961270413/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2961803126","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106707#issuecomment-2961803126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106707","id":2961803126,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6wiYd2","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-11T08:58:33Z","updated_at":"2025-06-11T08:58:33Z","body":"There is a proposal for that: https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1152\r\n\r\n> Should I also do an insert_icon_item to match add_icon_item for completeness?\r\n\r\n`add_icon_item()` is just `add_item()` with empty text 🤔I don't think it's needed that much.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2961803126/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3030181508","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106707#issuecomment-3030181508","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106707","id":3030181508,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60nOaE","user":{"login":"djdanlib","id":3030321,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzAzMjE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3030321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib","html_url":"https://github.com/djdanlib","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djdanlib/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-03T01:52:20Z","updated_at":"2025-07-03T01:52:20Z","body":"I just realized that I was meant to do the squashing. Sorry, I just took care of that, it should be all set now.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3030181508/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]